## Why This Is Asked
This question validates schema integrity across tenants, as drift can silently break analytics models. It assesses macro-based validation, multi-tenant RBAC, and CI integration capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- dbt macro design and information_schema usage
- Per-tenant schema validation and drift detection
- CI gates and test coverage (not_null/unique)
- PII masking and RLS in multi-tenant architectures

## Code Example
```sql
{% macro analytics_base.detect_schema_drift(tenant) %}
  {% set expected_columns = get_expected_columns(tenant) %}
  {% set actual_columns = run_query(
    "SELECT column_name FROM " ~ target.database ~ ".information_schema.columns " ~
    "WHERE table_schema = 'analytics_' ~ tenant " ~
    "AND table_name IN ('facts', 'events')"
  ) %}
  {% set actual_set = actual_columns.rows | map(attribute='column_name') | list %}
  {% set drift = [] %}
  {% for col in expected_columns %}
    {% if col.name not in actual_set %}
      {% set drift = drift.append('Missing: ' ~ col.name) %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
  {% if drift | length > 0 %}
    {{ exceptions.raise_compiler_error('Schema drift detected: ' ~ drift | join(', ')) }}
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
```

## Why This Matters
This interview question tests your understanding of macro correctness, multi-tenant schema templating, and CI/CD integration for data quality enforcement.

## Key Concepts
- dbt macros and singular/generic tests
- Per-tenant schemas using `analytics_{{tenant}}` naming convention
- CI gating: blocking deploys when any tenant's test reports NULL violations

## Code Example
```sql
-- analytics_base/macros/not_null_guard.sql
{% macro not_null_guard(tenant, model, col) %}
  (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM analytics_{{ tenant }}.{{ model }} WHERE {{ col }} IS NULL) = 0
{% endmacro %}
```

```sql
-- tests/generic/not_null_guard.sql
{% test not_null_guard(model, col) %}
  {% if execute %}
    {% set result = run_query(not_null_guard(this.name, model, col)) %}
    {% if result.rows[0][0] | int != 0 %}
      {% do exceptions.raise_compile_error(
        "Failed: " ~ model ~ "." ~ col ~ " contains NULL values"
      ) %}
    {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
{% endtest %}
```

The test verifies zero NULL values exist in the target column across all tenant-specific models.
